.TH EXPIRY 1 "" "expiry" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
expiry \- track expiring secrets, certificates and anything else, with email reminders
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B expiry
.RI [ \-c " FILE" ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.br
.B expiry
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help | \-V | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B expiry
keeps a list of
.I reminders
\(em things that expire: application secrets, certificates, licenses, domains, tokens.
Each reminder has a name, an expiry date, the number of days left and optional notes.
.PP
A background service (the Docker container) keeps the list up to date and sends
notifications
.B 30 days, 14 days and 1 day
before each expiry date, plus on the expiry day itself (all configurable).
Reminders are created in three ways:
.IP \(bu 3
.B Manually
with
.BR "expiry add" .
.IP \(bu 3
.B Entra ID
(Azure AD): client secrets and certificates of every app registration (and optionally
enterprise applications) are imported automatically by
.BR "expiry sync" .
.IP \(bu 3
.B SSL/TLS
certificates: the certificate served by a domain or IP is read directly from the
server, see
.BR "expiry ssl" .
.PP
On the server, the
.B expiry
command is a small wrapper that runs the CLI inside the
.I expiry
container with
.BR "docker exec" ,
so every command below works the same when connected over SSH.
.SH DATES
Wherever a DATE is expected you can use the configured
.I date_format
(default
.BR DD/MM/YYYY ,
e.g. 31/03/2027),
.BR YYYY\-MM\-DD ,
or a date relative to today:
.BR +30d ", " +2w ", " +6m ", " +1y .
Dates are displayed in
.I date_format
and in the configured
.I timezone
(e.g. Europe/Dublin); JSON and export output always use YYYY\-MM\-DD.
.SH REMINDER COMMANDS
.TP
.BR "list " "[" \-a "] [" \-s " SOURCE] [" \-w " DAYS] [" \-e "] [" \-q " TEXT] [" \-\-json ]
List active reminders, soonest first, with the days left (color coded).
.B \-a
also shows archived/ignored ones,
.B \-s
filters by source
.RB ( manual ", " entra ", " ssl ),
.B \-w
shows only items expiring within DAYS days,
.B \-e
only expired items,
.B \-q
searches name and notes. Alias:
.BR ls .
.TP
.BR "add " "NAME DATE [NOTES...] [" \-n " TEXT] [" \-\-notify " EMAIL] [" \-\-mute ]
Add a reminder. Everything after DATE is stored as notes (or use
.BR \-n ).
.B \-\-notify
adds extra recipients for this reminder only (repeatable or comma separated).
.TP
.BR "show " ID " [" \-\-json ]
Show every field of a reminder, its recipients, the notification schedule
(sent / scheduled / skipped) and recent notifications.
.TP
.BR "edit " "ID [" \-\-name " N] [" \-d " DATE] [" \-n " NOTES] [" \-\-append\-note " T] [" \-\-notify " E] [" \-\-add\-notify " E] [" \-\-clear\-notify "] [" \-\-mute | \-\-unmute ]
Edit a reminder. With no options it asks for each field interactively.
Changing the date (a renewal) restarts the notification cycle.
For synced reminders (entra, ssl) name and date are refreshed by the next sync;
notes, recipients and mute are kept.
.TP
.BR "rm " "ID [ID...] [" \-y ]
Remove reminders (asks for confirmation unless
.BR \-y ).
Manual reminders are deleted. Synced reminders are marked
.I ignored
so they are not re-imported. Aliases:
.BR remove ", " delete .
.TP
.BR "restore " ID
Re-activate an ignored or archived reminder.
.SH SSL COMMANDS
.TP
.BR "ssl add " "HOST[:PORT]... [" \-\-sni " NAME] [" \-\-name " N] [" \-n " NOTES] [" \-f ]
Start tracking the certificate served by one or more hosts (domain, IPv4, IPv6 or a URL;
default port 443). Use
.B \-\-sni
when HOST is an IP but the server needs a host name to pick the certificate.
The certificate is read immediately and a reminder is created; self-signed and
expired certificates are supported.
.B \-f
adds the host even if it cannot be reached right now.
.TP
.BR "ssl list " [ \-\-json ]
List tracked hosts with their reminder, expiry date, days left and issuer.
.TP
.BR "ssl rm " "TARGET|HOST[:PORT] [" \-\-sni " NAME]"
Stop tracking a host (the reminder is archived).
.TP
.BR "ssl check " "HOST[:PORT] [" \-\-sni " NAME] [" \-\-json ]
Inspect a certificate now without saving anything: subject, issuer, validity,
days left, whether it is trusted, SANs, serial and fingerprint.
.TP
.BR "ssl discover " "DOMAIN [" \-\-add "] [" \-p " PORT] [" \-y ]
Find host names under DOMAIN from public Certificate Transparency logs (crt.sh),
connect to each one and show its certificate expiry.
.B \-\-add
starts tracking every reachable host that is not tracked yet.
.TP
.BR "ssl scan " "[" \-d " DOMAIN] [" \-n " NAME] [" \-\-names\-file " FILE|\-] [" \-\-network " CIDR] [" \-p " PORTS] [" \-\-wildcards "] [" \-\-add "] [" \-y ]
Find where your certificates are installed, including wildcard certificates on several
servers. Tries about 180 typical host names under each domain (plus \fB\-\-name\fR values,
names from \fB\-\-names\-file\fR \(em a plain list or a Windows/BIND DNS export; \fB\-\fR reads
stdin \(em and public names from certificate logs) using this server's DNS, optionally every
address of the \fB\-\-network\fR ranges, on ports 443, 8443 and 9443 unless \fB\-\-ports\fR is
given, and reads each server's certificate with a TLS handshake (nothing else is sent). Keeps certificates issued for the domains and groups them by certificate.
.B \-\-add
tracks the new locations. Defaults come from \fIsources.ssl.scan\fR, which also runs the
scan on a schedule (\fIadd: true\fR tracks new finds automatically and emails a summary).
Tell your network/security team before scanning networks.
.SH SYNC AND NOTIFICATION COMMANDS
.TP
.BR "sync " "[" \-s " entra|ssl] [" \-\-dry\-run ]
Pull expiry dates from the enabled sources now. New credentials become reminders,
changed dates are updated, and credentials that no longer exist are archived.
Runs automatically on the
.I schedule.sync
cron schedule.
.TP
.BR "check " [ \-\-dry\-run ]
Send the notifications that are due now. Each stage is sent once per reminder and
expiry date; failed deliveries are retried at the next check. Runs automatically on the
.I schedule.check
cron schedule.
.TP
.BR "test\-notify " "[" \-\-to " EMAIL] [" \-\-no\-email "] [" \-\-no\-webhooks ]
Send a sample notification to verify email / webhook settings.
.TP
.BR "status " [ \-\-json ]
Show whether the service is running, the schedule, last and next sync/check,
enabled sources and channels, counts and configuration problems.
.TP
.BR "history " "[" \-i " ID] [" \-n " N] [" \-\-json ]
Notifications sent or failed.
.TP
.BR "audit " "[" \-i " ID] [" \-n " N] [" \-\-json ]
Change log: who added, edited or removed what (the SSH user name is recorded),
and changes made by syncs. Alias:
.BR log .
.SH ADMIN COMMANDS
.TP
.BR "config show"
Print the effective configuration with secrets masked.
.TP
.BR "config check " [ \-\-connect ]
Validate the configuration;
.B \-\-connect
also signs in to Entra ID and verifies the Graph permission.
.TP
.BR "export " "[" \-f " json|csv] [" \-a "] [" \-o " FILE]"
Export reminders (backup, spreadsheets).
.TP
.BR "import " "FILE|\-  [" \-\-dry\-run ]
Import manual reminders from JSON (the export format) or CSV with a header
.BR name,expires_on[,notes,notify,muted] .
Existing name + date pairs are skipped.
.TP
.BR "backup create " "[" \-d " DIR]"
Back up the database now (a consistent snapshot, safe while the service runs).
The daemon does this automatically every night (\fIbackup.schedule\fR) and keeps
the newest \fIbackup.keep\fR files.
.TP
.BR "backup list " "[" \-d " DIR]"
List backups, newest first.
.TP
.BR "backup restore " "FILE [" \-y ]
Replace the current data with a backup (a file name from \fBbackup list\fR or a path).
The current database is saved first as \fIexpiry\-prerestore\-<time>.db\fR.
.TP
.BR "entra cert\-create " "[" \-\-path " FILE] [" \-\-days " N] [" \-f ]
Create a private key and self\-signed certificate for signing in to Entra ID
instead of a client secret. Writes \fI/data/entra\-auth.pem\fR (key + certificate,
mode 600) and \fI/data/entra\-auth.crt\fR (public certificate to upload to the app
registration). Then set \fIentra.certificate_path\fR.
.TP
.BR "entra cert\-show " "[" \-\-path " FILE] [" \-\-pem ]
Show the login certificate's thumbprint and expiry;
.B \-\-pem
prints the public certificate.
.TP
.B daemon
Run the scheduler in the foreground (the container's default command).
.TP
.B health
Exit 0 when the daemon heartbeat is recent (Docker HEALTHCHECK).
.TP
.B install
Copy the host wrapper, this man page and a starter configuration to the host
(run through
.BR "docker run" ,
see INSTALLATION).
.TP
.BR "help " [ COMMAND ...]
Show help;
.B expiry COMMAND \-\-help
works too.
.SH NOTIFICATIONS
Stages are taken from
.I notify.days_before
(default 30, 14, 1) plus the expiry day when
.I notify.on_expiry_day
is true. A reminder is due for the tightest stage it has reached; looser stages that
were missed are skipped, so an item added with 5 days left gets one email, not three.
Recipients are
.I notify.emails
plus the reminder's own
.B \-\-notify
addresses plus, for Entra apps with
.IR sources.entra.notify_owners ,
the app owners.
In
.I individual
mode each item is emailed separately; in
.I digest
mode each recipient gets one email per run listing all their due items.
Webhooks (Slack, Teams Workflows, generic JSON) get one message per run.
.SH SELF\-MONITORING
After every job the daemon checks its own health. When the Entra or SSL sync fails
\fIalerts.sync_failures\fR times in a row (default 3), or a reminder could not be
delivered, or a backup failed, an alert is sent to \fIalerts.emails\fR (default
\fInotify.emails\fR) and to every webhook, repeated every \fIalerts.repeat_hours\fR
(default 24) while it lasts, followed by a RESOLVED message. \fBexpiry status\fR shows
the current health.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/expiry/config.yaml
Main configuration (mounted read-only into the container as
.IR /config/config.yaml ).
.TP
.I /etc/expiry/expiry.env
Secrets passed to the container with
.BR \-\-env\-file ;
referenced from the config as
.IR ${NAME} .
.TP
.I /etc/expiry/templates/reminder.html.j2
Copy of the default email template; set
.I email.template_file
to use a customized one.
.TP
.I expiry-data:/data/expiry.db
SQLite database in the Docker volume
.IR expiry\-data .
.TP
.I /var/backups/expiry
Nightly backups when mounted at \fI/backups\fR (otherwise \fI/data/backups\fR).
.TP
.I expiry-data:/data/entra-auth.pem
Entra login key + certificate created by \fBentra cert\-create\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EXPIRY_CONFIG
Config file path (default /config/config.yaml).
.TP
.B EXPIRY_DB
Database path (overrides
.IR database ).
.TP
.B EXPIRY_CONTAINER
Container name used by the host wrapper (default expiry).
.TP
.B EXPIRY_DOCKER
Docker command used by the host wrapper (default docker, e.g. "sudo docker" or podman).
.SH INSTALLATION
.nf
docker run \-\-rm \-u 0 \e
  \-v /usr/local/bin:/host/bin \e
  \-v /usr/local/share/man/man1:/host/man \e
  \-v /etc/expiry:/host/config \e
  ghcr.io/devlossantos/expiry:latest install

install \-d \-o 10001 \-g 10001 \-m 750 /var/backups/expiry

docker run \-d \-\-name expiry \-\-restart unless\-stopped \e
  \-\-log\-opt max\-size=10m \-\-log\-opt max\-file=5 \e
  \-\-env\-file /etc/expiry/expiry.env \e
  \-v /etc/expiry:/config:ro \-v expiry\-data:/data \e
  \-v /var/backups/expiry:/backups ghcr.io/devlossantos/expiry:latest
.fi
.PP
Users need access to Docker (member of the
.I docker
group, or use sudo) to run the wrapper.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
expiry add "Payroll API cert" 31/03/2027 renew via DigiCert portal
expiry add github\-pat +90d \-\-notify dev@example.com
expiry list \-w 30
expiry edit 7 \-\-date 31/03/2028
expiry rm 7
expiry ssl add example.com mail.example.com:993
expiry ssl add 10.0.0.15 \-\-sni portal.example.com
expiry ssl discover example.com \-\-add
expiry sync \-\-dry\-run
expiry check \-\-dry\-run
expiry export \-f csv > reminders.csv
expiry backup list
expiry entra cert\-create
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on errors (e.g. a failed sync or notification), 2 on usage errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docker (1),
.BR crontab (5)
